{"id":"resp_aec1e34b0b5149a6","created_at":1795550730,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9fbaaccdbebe98bf","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shapes for the requirement TRF-035 clause 4.1.1: \"L shall be taken as the ship's rule length used by the classification society.\"\n\nWe have ontology terms: classificationSocietyRuleLength (ObjectProperty linking benchmarkEntity to QuantityValue), ruleLength (ObjectProperty linking benchmarkEntity to QuantityValue). Also classificationSociety (DatatypeProperty) but not needed. Also hullRegion, bowRegion etc not needed.\n\nWe need to represent that for each ship, there must be a ruleLength value that corresponds to L, and classificationSocietyRuleLength representing L used by classification society. The requirement says: L shall be taken as the ship's rule length used by the classification society. So L equals classificationSocietyRuleLength? Actually classificationSocietyRuleLength is defined as \"Classification society rule length\". So L is that quantity. The ruleLength property is also rule length for benchmark entity? Might be generic rule length. But we want shape to ensure that a ship has a classificationSocietyRuleLength quantity value, with unit meters, numeric.\n\nWe need to use quantityEncoding predicates: numeric_predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue; unit_predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit. So in SHACL we can define constraints that the object of classificationSocietyRuleLength must be a QUDT QuantityValue having those properties.\n\nDefine a shape targeting ship class (owner_class). Use sh:targetClass with ship IRI.\n\nAdd property shapes:\n\n- sh:property for classificationSocietyRuleLength:\n  - sh:path classificationSocietyRuleLength\n  - sh:nodeKind sh:IRI (or sh:BlankNodeOrIRI) because it's a QuantityValue.\n  - sh:property for numeric value: we can use sh:property inside a node shape for the quantity? Simpler: define a node shape for QUDT QuantityValue with sh:targetObjectsOf classificationSocietyRuleLength, but recommend pattern:\n\nDefine a shape for quantity values: maybe define a node shape with targetObjectsOf classificationSocietyRuleLength that enforces that it has qudt:numericValue of datatype xsd:decimal and qudt:unit of unit M.\n\nBut we also need ruleLength? The requirement just about L taken as the ship's rule length used by classification society. So could enforce that ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength refer to same value? Or that ruleLength is present and equal to classificationSocietyRuleLength? The requirement states L is the rule length used by classification society. So there is only classificationSocietyRuleLength; ruleLength may represent L across other contexts. Possibly need to enforce that ruleLength value equals classificationSocietyRuleLength (i.e., same QuantityValue). Could enforce using sh:equals or sh:hasValue? In SHACL, sh:equals is between two property paths on same node. So we can require that (ship) classificationSocietyRuleLength and ruleLength have same value (same IRI). Use sh:property with sh:path [ sh:equals??]. Actually sh:equals is a constraint to compare two values of same node; using sh:equals points to a property path that must have same set of values. So we can have property shape for ruleLength with sh:path ruleLength, sh:equals classificationSocietyRuleLength.\n\nThus ensure they are same.\n\nImplement shapes:\n\n- ex:ShipShape a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass vocab:ship; then property shapes.\n\nDefine prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, xsd, qudt, vocab.\n\nProvide URIs exactly.\n\nImplement quantity validation:\n\nDefine a shape ex:QuantityShape targeting objects of classificationSocietyRuleLength and ruleLength (i.e., sh:targetObjectsOf). Inside, enforce numericValue with datatype decimal, unit must be qudt:unit with value http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M (maybe use sh:hasValue). But as we cannot assert specific unit? requirement says unit meters. So enforce unit equals M.\n\nThus:\n\nex:QuantityShape a sh:NodeShape;\n  sh:targetObjectsOf vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength, vocab:ruleLength;\n  sh:property [\n    sh:path qudt:numericValue;\n    sh:datatype xsd:decimal;\n    sh:minCount 1;\n    sh:maxCount 1;\n  ];\n  sh:property [\n    sh:path qudt:unit;\n    sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M>;\n    sh:minCount 1;\n    sh:maxCount 1;\n  ].\n\nThen ShipShape:\n\nex:ShipShape a sh:NodeShape;\n  sh:targetClass vocab:ship;\n  sh:property [\n    sh:path vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength;\n    sh:minCount 1;\n    sh:node ex:QuantityShape;   // but node expects shape; could embed inline shape or use sh:node ex:QuantityShape.\n  ];\n  sh:property [\n    sh:path vocab:ruleLength;\n    sh:minCount 1;\n    sh:node ex:QuantityShape;\n    sh:equals vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength;\n  ].\n\nBut sh:equals expects property shape, not node shape. Actually in sh:property you can include sh:equals referencing another property path on the same node (the ship). So for ruleLength property shape, include sh:equals vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength.\n\nAlternatively could have just one property shape for classificationSocietyRuleLength and use that as L. But ruleLength may be redundant. Yet we include both to capture equality.\n\nMake sure we don't invent owners: we target ship as per contract owner. That's allowed.\n\nNo data about classificationSociety property.\n\nThus produce SHACL.\n\nNeed to include full Turtle with prefixes.\n\nAdd comment that unresolved ownership not present.\n\nReturn lines <BEGIN_SHACL> and <END_SHACL>.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_bc191ff7b28f6751","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/shapes#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that validates any QUDT QuantityValue used for rule lengths\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:QuantityShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetObjectsOf vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength , vocab:ruleLength ;\n    \n    # The quantity must have a numeric value (decimal)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # The quantity must be expressed in metres\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Ship shape – enforces presence of the required length quantities\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    \n    # L (the rule length used by the classification society) must be present\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node ex:QuantityShape ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # The generic ruleLength property must also be present and must be the same\n    # quantity as the classificationSocietyRuleLength (L = ruleLength)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:ruleLength ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node ex:QuantityShape ;\n        sh:equals vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":41966,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":41360,"input_tokens_per_turn":[41966],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1716,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1217,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1716],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":43682},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}